00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:58.890
<v Cris Beam>Do you think that girls are critical of each other? Because it seems to me when I see them on the street, there's a whole lot of criticism if one doesn't look the right way or one doesn't fit into a certain image.
<v Cris Beam>你认为女孩们对彼此苛刻吗？因为在我看来，当我在街上看到她们时，如果一个人看起来不对劲或不符合某种形象，就会受到很多批评。

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:27.150
<v Foxxjazell>I'll say this about myself. I do feel insecure sometimes if I go out with another girl that isn't as passable as I am. Because for one thing, it's bad enough if you get clocked. But if you're with another girl that is not passable that's going to get you clocked even more, that brings your self-esteem down. So a lot of girls and even myself, won't even go out in public with less passable girls. Or girls that are going to bring ridicule to them.
<v Foxxjazell>我对自己这么说。如果我和另一个不如我通关率高的女孩一起出去，有时会感到不安。因为首先，被抓包已经够糟糕了。但如果你和另一个不合格的女孩在一起，会让你更容易被抓包，这会降低你的自尊心。所以很多女孩，甚至我自己，甚至不会和那些不合格的女孩一起出现在公共场合。或者那些会给她们招致嘲笑的女孩。

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:29.560
<v Cris Beam>That seems pretty harsh.
<v Cris Beam>这似乎太苛刻了。

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:55.750
<v Foxxjazell>It's harsh, but you have to realize. I mean, being a transgender woman is bad enough, so why would you want to put more gasoline on the fire?
<v Foxxjazell>很苛刻，但你必须意识到。我的意思是，做一个变性女性已经够糟糕了，所以为什么还要火上浇油呢？

00:13:55.750 --> 00:14:16.070
<v Cris Beam>There's a certain strip of Santa Monica Boulevard in Hollywood that Foxx says is famous worldwide. It's where straight, often married men, come to pick up young, transgender prostitutes. It's also where just out transgender kids often first spot their own kind and can imagine a place to blend in. They hang out at Benito's, an all-night taco stand.
