<v Foxxjazell>不。

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.750
<v Woman>Oh, OK. I was going to say--
<v Woman>哦，好的。我本来想说——

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:07.010
<v Foxxjazell>It's been so long since I've seen you.
<v Foxxjazell>好久没见到你了。

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:23.850
<v Cris Beam>Girls who have just derived in LA might show up here to socialize for a few weeks, and then turn a trick for some cash. It's by then that they've learned how hard it is to get a legitimate job when you're 17 and have both a male ID and C cup breasts. So sex work becomes the option.
<v Cris Beam>刚到洛杉矶的女孩可能会来这里社交几周，然后为了钱接客。到那时她们才知道，当你17岁，既有男性身份证又有C罩杯乳房时，找到一份合法的工作有多难。所以性工作成了选择。

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:34.020
<v Cris Beam>It can be dangerous, especially for the younger girls. Some of whom have been kicked out by their parents at 13 or 14, and are looking for a place to stay when they're talking to johns.
<v Cris Beam>这可能很危险，尤其是对年轻女孩来说。她们中有些人在13或14岁时就被父母赶了出来，在和嫖客交谈时还在寻找住处。

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:37.580
<v Cris Beam>Foxx used to work with the Boulevard, but now she's moved onto office jobs.
<v Cris Beam>Foxx过去常在大道工作，但现在她转行做办公室工作了。

00:15:37.580 --> 00:16:08.170
<v Foxxjazell>Whenever I do work the Boulevard, whenever I have to work the Boulevard, I have a purpose in mind. And that's to get money for that point in time, whether it's to booked studio time, or whatever. And most of the time I really try to stay away from the Boulevard. I haven't worked it in a long while. Especially since I've had a stable job. Basically, it's something that all of us girls have to do because for one thing, we're not sought after as like, the number one type of employee.
<v Foxxjazell>每当我在大道工作，每当我不得不去大道工作时，我都有一个目的。那就是为了那个时间段的钱，无论是为了付录音室的费用，还是其他什么。大多数时候我真的尽量远离大道。我已经很久没在那工作了。特别是在有了稳定工作之后。基本上，这是我们所有女孩都不得不做的事，因为首先，我们并不是那种最受追捧的员工类型。

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:12.530
<v Cris Beam>What is it like trying to get a job as a young, transgender person?
<v Cris Beam>作为一名年轻的变性人，找工作是什么感觉？

00:16:12.530 --> 00:17:00.000
<v Foxxjazell>It can be very frustrating. Because I would say that the last couple of jobs I've been at-- last couple jobs, I've had a big problem with using the women's restroom. It's like, genetic women, they can be very supportive for transgender women as far as our whole transition, helping us out with our makeup, giving us tips on men. But it's like when it comes to the bathroom, that's like off limits. It's like, we've just intruded their personal space and I don't understand that. And the last two jobs I was at, a lot of women had a problem with we using the women's restroom. And I'm like, OK, I look like a woman. I'm build like a woman. I have breasts like a woman. And you want me to go use the men's restroom?
<v Foxxjazell>这可能非常令人沮丧。因为我想说，我过去两份工作——过去两份工作，我在使用女厕所方面遇到了很大的问题。就像，生理女性，她们在整个转变过程中可以非常支持变性女性，帮助我们化妆，给我们一些关于男人的建议。但当涉及到厕所时，那是禁区。就像，我们侵犯了她们的个人空间，我不明白这一点。我过去的两份工作中，很多女性对我们使用女厕所都有意见。而我觉得，好吧，我看起来像个女人。我的身材像个女人。我有像女人一样的乳房。而你想要我去用男厕所？

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:23.560
<v Foxxjazell>If anything, that's going to mess up a little kid. Just imagine some little boy going to the restroom and he sees this really nice-looking Jennifer Lopez look-alike woman standing up urinating at the urinal. That's going to just destroy his whole mind concept.
<v Foxxjazell>如果非要那样，那会毁了一个小孩子的。想象一下，某个小男孩走进厕所，看到这个看起来很像詹妮弗·洛佩兹的女人站在小便池前小便。那会彻底摧毁他的心智概念。

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:38.720
<v Cris Beam>The girls on Santa Monica can make $200, $300 in a night, but will talk surprisingly casually about their job. For some, there's a bit of a thrill to tantalizing the straight men who would normally rebuff them. And for others, it's an unfortunate pause on the path to day work.
<v Cris Beam>圣莫尼卡大道上的女孩们一晚上能赚200、300美元，但谈论她们的工作时却出奇地随意。对一些人来说，挑逗那些通常会拒绝她们的异性恋男人有一点刺激。而对另一些人来说，这是通往日常工作道路上的一次不幸停顿。

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:56.890
<v Foxxjazell>So many girls come to Santa Monica Boulevard and they have that Pretty Woman concept that oh, I'm going to go out here and work the Boulevard. I'm going to meet a Richard Gere look-alike and he's going to be a millionaire. And he's going to marry me and we're going to have children. I think that's what a lot of girls really think. They have that Pretty Woman concept.
<v Foxxjazell>很多女孩来到圣莫尼卡大道时，都有那种《风月俏佳人》的观念，噢，我要到这里来在这条大道上工作。我会遇到一个长得像理查·基尔的人，他会是个百万富翁。他会娶我，我们会生孩子。我想很多女孩真的这么想。她们有那种《风月俏佳人》的观念。

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.320
<v Cris Beam>Do you have that fantasy?
<v Cris Beam>你有那种幻想吗？

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:11.650
<v Foxxjazell>I tend to have that fantasy from time to time. And I've actually met a couple of men on the Boulevard that have a little money and they want to spend on me.
<v Foxxjazell>我不时会有那种幻想。而且我实际上在大道上遇到过几个有点钱的男人，他们想为我花钱。

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:20.640
<v Foxxjazell>Everyone, come on. Everybody in the arena come on and watch me do my thing. Watch me do my thing. I like to do my thing.
<v Foxxjazell>大家，来吧。竞技场里的每一个人，来看着我做我的事。看着我做我的事。我喜欢做我的事。

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:33.780
<v Cris Beam>It's Friday night at Foxx's tiny studio apartment. And while Foxx sings and raps with her friend [UNINTELLIGIBLE], two of her drag daughters, 15 year old Angela and 18 year old Ariel, are getting ready to go dancing at an underage club.
<v Cris Beam>这是Foxx那间狭小的单身公寓里的周五晚上。当Foxx和她的朋友们一起唱歌说唱时，她的两个变装女儿，15岁的Angela和18岁的Ariel，正准备去一个未成年人俱乐部跳舞。

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:45.600
<v Cris Beam>Luckily, both kids are petite and the onset of puberty has been slow. Their faces are soft and in their clingy nylon dresses, bobbed wigs and knee high boots, they pass amazingly well.
<v Cris Beam>幸运的是，两个孩子都很娇小，而且青春期开始得较慢。她们的面孔柔和，穿着紧身的尼龙裙、波波头假发和及膝靴，她们的女性形象看起来非常真实。

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:51.630
<v Cris Beam>They dress like any Latina high schooler in LA would-- baby doll cute-- but a little more trampy than a mom would like.
<v Cris Beam>她们的穿着就像洛杉矶任何一个拉丁裔高中生一样——可爱的小洋娃娃装——但比妈妈们喜欢的稍微风骚一点。

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:57.150
<v Ariel>Do I look pretty? Do I look pretty?
<v Ariel>我看起来漂亮吗？我看起来漂亮吗？

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:59.910
<v Foxxjazell>Does she look pretty? Yes you do.
<v Foxxjazell>她看起来漂亮吗？是的，你很漂亮。

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:26.860
<v Cris Beam>Angela and Ariel, like a handful of other local kids, keep their wigs, heels, handbags, and makeup at Foxx's. Angela and Ariel both still go to high school and live at boys during the day, and don't want to risk getting caught by their families. While some of the other teens who live on the streets just don't want to get their stuff stolen. So Foxx's place is a sort of de facto dressing room come clubhouse, where kids come in and out to dress up, eat Foxx's food, get some motherly advice, and often crash on her couch.
<v Cris Beam>Angela和Ariel，像其他一些当地孩子一样，把她们的假发、高跟鞋、手提包和化妆品存放在Foxx那里。Angela和Ariel白天都还在上高中，以男孩的身份生活，不想冒被家人发现的风险。而一些流浪在街头的青少年则只是不想让自己的东西被偷。所以Foxx的住处是一个事实上的更衣室兼俱乐部，孩子们进进出出进行打扮，吃Foxx的食物，得到一些像母亲一样的建议，并经常在她的沙发上过夜。

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:36.540
<v Cris Beam>I was there for hours watching them do and re-do their makeup, primp and fluff and gaze into the mirror. And pull an astonishing number of gogo boots out of Foxx's closet.
<v Cris Beam>我在那里呆了几个小时，看着她们化妆、卸妆、打扮、整理，对着镜子凝视。并从Foxx的衣柜里拿出数量惊人的Go-go靴。

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:46.580
<v Foxxjazell>You don't have a bra on? You can put the water balloons, so they can look big and soft. At the same time when you walk, they'll move.
<v Foxxjazell>你没穿内衣吗？你可以放水球进去，这样它们看起来又大又软。同时当你走动时，它们会动。

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:56.220
<v Cris Beam>They fill their bras with water balloons. Hormones would get them breast in a matter of months and would add weight to their narrow hips and backsides. But for now, neither has started taking.
